From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: attrr <110731994+attrr@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 18:09:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] interconnect: qcom: sm8150: Enable sync_state

Add the generic icc sync_state callback, which b95b668eaaa2 dropped
from sm8150 and sm8250 alike and bfc7db1cb94a brought back to sm8250
only: without it every node stays at its initial INT_MAX bandwidth, DDR
and the NoCs included, and the SoC never reaches system sleep (CXSD).

Fixes: b95b668eaaa2 ("interconnect: qcom: icc-rpmh: Add BCMs to commit list in pre_aggregate")
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/interconnect/qcom/sm8150.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/interconnect/qcom/sm8150.c b/drivers/interconnect/qcom/sm8150.c
index ae732afbd155..d4ffe5b2452a 100644
--- a/drivers/interconnect/qcom/sm8150.c
+++ b/drivers/interconnect/qcom/sm8150.c
@@ -1852,6 +1852,7 @@ static struct platform_driver qnoc_driver = {
 	.driver = {
 		.name = "qnoc-sm8150",
 		.of_match_table = qnoc_of_match,
+		.sync_state = icc_sync_state,
 	},
 };
 module_platform_driver(qnoc_driver);
